{"kind":"report","text":"At main74384558, clone portability is only partially planned and not delivered. Current room authority is per-scope Durable Object journals/retained inputs; Git has published files and publication receipt commits under refs/artroom/receipts/\u003chash\u003e (docs/architecture.md:153–177), not complete issue/change journals. dap clone currently runs ordinary git clone with a minted read token (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:1269–1278); current replay CLI uses the HTTP source and has no --git path (packages/replay/src/cli.ts:19–22).\n\nReviewed notes/2026-10-09-shared-language-volatile-acts.md sections15/16 plan asynchronous archive per scope under refs/artroom/journal/\u003cscope\u003e, segments/manifests/retained inputs, Git-backed replay, archive progress and live archive→clone→offline replay acceptance. Current NOW P1 parent e871ba09 remains promised55d9a12f. Delivered A0a explicit recorded-level foundation and A1a internal path/ref codec only; notes/2026-10-15-archive-path-grammar.md explicitly says no export/runtime/archive enabled. Layout/dependency/privacy inventory, writer, Git reader, progress and real archive acceptance remain owed. DO stays live sequencer; planned refs are portable journal replicas, not gitseq-style primary event authority.\n\nThe existing plan falls short of Hugh's complete portable room state:\n1. It explicitly omits retained text (§15.1/15.3); issue bodies and comments are detached text (issue.ts:42,174). Digests alone cannot reconstruct readable content. --texts is planned as separate supplied bytes, not clone-complete content. Complete authorized payload export requires revisiting the deliberate prior omission, including redaction/access semantics.\n2. Per-scope archives may lag independently. A room export needs discovery/complete scope inventory, captured heads with dependency closure, pinned definitions/versioned rules, required content/artifacts, explicit omissions and completeness/freshness evidence. A prefix verified consistent is not proof of latest state everywhere; the plan excludes shared register/inboxes and does not currently archive the complete directory root as a whole-room snapshot.\n3. Ordinary remote git clone does not fetch arbitrary custom refs. CLI lacks journal-ref fetch plumbing; choose explicit dap clone refspecs or archive reachability under normally fetched refs if plain git clone itself must suffice. Official git-clone documents normal branch refs vs mirror all refs.\n4. Git-backed verification is planned, but supported offline room reconstruction/browsing/import is additional work: verify reports coverage and trusts, not a complete room product view.\n5. Continuing the same authoritative room elsewhere needs a distinct migration/restore contract. Archive omits outbox/dispatcher marks/sessions/credentials/folded state (§15.3). Folded items may be rederived, but a sent external mutation with lost reply cannot safely be treated as unsent. Need old-writer fencing, identity/incarnation and ownership treatment, authoritative bindings/credential replacement, pending-operation reconciliation, cutover and recovery. Do not put private signing keys or provider secrets in repository just to make data portable. Existing task/agent save/restore plans do not establish this room protocol.\n6. Existing earlier rooms do not gain archive automatically; §15.2 explicitly says new platform versions and no migration owed. Complete portability for present demo rooms needs a supported enablement/export/backfill decision.\n\nRecommended acceptance boundary for design discussion: capture a room's export cut; include complete authorized non-redacted issue/change payloads and dependency closure; clone through the promised user command; make original service unavailable; discover/reconstruct/browse all included issues, discussions, change versions and relationships locally with explicit cutoff/omissions; verify against retained heads. Writable rehosting is separately specified if desired. Waiting for that selected clone/export cut can preserve asynchronous normal acts; it does not require Git-before-answer for every act.\n\nThe present demo claim overstates delivered storage. Accurate current wording: 'Issues and changes live in dap's journals; published files and publication receipts are in Git. Cloneable journal archives are in development.' No demo edit, source implementation, provider operation or builder reprioritization performed. This is a read-only gap explanation, not authorization to change the existing detached-text policy or commission migration.\n"}